        "title": "Slope Stability: Limit Equilibrium, Bishop Method, Seismic Stability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Slopes fail when driving forces (gravity component along failure surface) exceed resisting forces (shear strength along the surface). Limit equilibrium methods find the ratio of available shear strength to mobilized shear stress — the factor of safety — along a trial failure surface. The minimum F over all possible surfaces determines stability."
